# SELECT50 example: UMA-S-1.1 IRC in both directions from a converged TS.
#
# SETUP
# Install ORCA 6 and ORCA External Tools with UMA support as described at the
# top of job_orca.inp: https://github.com/faccts/orca-external-tools
# Replace ProgExt with the full installed oet_client path (.exe on Windows).
# Start the server in another terminal and leave it running:
#   oet_server uma -b 127.0.0.1:20001 -n 4
# Adjust the CPU allocation and cuda/cpu selection for your installation.
#
# RUN
# First finish the companion job_orca_ts.inp optimization/frequency calculation.
# Check that the TS has one chemically relevant imaginary mode. Copy its FINAL
# job_orca_ts.xyz and matching job_orca_ts.hess into a fresh IRC job directory.
# Keep atom ordering, geometry, charge/multiplicity and model identical to the
# TS/frequency calculation. Edit the filenames below if your TS used another name.
#   /path/to/orca job_orca_irc.inp > job_orca_irc.out 2>&1
# Windows PowerShell:
#   & "C:/path/to/orca.exe" job_orca_irc.inp > job_orca_irc.out 2>&1
#
# If no matching final Hessian is available, replace InitHess read with
# InitHess calc_numfreq and remove Hess_Filename to calculate it at the input TS.
# MaxIter 100 is an example allowance; check whether either direction hits it.
# Inspect job_orca_irc_IRC_Full_trj.xyz and both path endpoints. Optimize the
# endpoints separately with job_orca.inp and check their identity/frequencies.
# Forward/backward labels do not by themselves identify reactant and product.
# This is a derived template, not an original record of a deposited IRC.
# IRC keywords: https://www.faccts.de/docs/orca/6.1/manual/contents/structurereactivity/irc.html
#
! ExtOpt IRC

%method
  ProgExt "/path/to/oet_client"
  Ext_Params "-b 127.0.0.1:20001 --model uma-s-1p1 --task omol --device cuda"
end

%pal
  nprocs 4
end

%irc
  Direction both
  MaxIter 100
  InitHess read
  Hess_Filename "job_orca_ts.hess"
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job_orca_ts.xyz
